ata; flag for reviewer. Conflict: CNBC 2022 says July 2022 was \"Google's first cash investment\"; the S-4 shows a Google warrant under a 2017 services agreement. Government grants: S-4 says TAE \"has received over eight awards from the United States' Department of Energy\" without amounts or dates; no ARPA-E / SBIR / Milestone award found in earlier probes (probes/arpa-e.md, sbir.md, doe-programs.md); INFUSE page snapshot is JS-heavy and had no TAE hit; USAspending not queried (POST API, no archived wrapper available). No DOE grant event recorded: revisit. Not recorded: Linqto Liquidshares secondary vehicle (Form D 2023/2024, secondary, not company funding). WebSearch budget was exhausted so TAE Life Sciences, Rusnano 2012 and 2007 round details come from Wikipedia/GeekWire only. TMTG merger not closed as of the S-4 (expected Q4 2026). VERIFIER (2026-10-05): Series 12 counting now = tae-series-12-fy2025 ($146.6M) + tae-series-12-fy2026 ($56.8M) = $203.4M; the SAFE event ($97.6M, converted into Series 12 inside the $146.6M) and the June 2025 \">$150M\" release are marked duplicate of tae-series-12-fy2025. Cash timing: SAFE cash came in FY2024-25 ($29.7M of SAFE proceeds in FY2025 cash flow), so the S-4 figures are booked at Series 12 dates rather than when the SAFE cash arrived. tae-series-12-fy2026 announced_on 2025-04-01 is a fiscal-period placeholder (S-4 gives only the fiscal year), not a release date. The TMTG May 2025 PIPE / $1B convertible notes are TMTG's own financing and are NOT TAE funding. The merger is all-stock (no cash to TAE at close per the 8-K); the \">$6B\" CNBC figure is the headline deal value and may describe the transaction rather than TAE's standalone valuation. The 2023 TAE Power Solutions, LLC Series A units were sold by a subsidiary (consolidated; recorded as noncontrolling interest, $61.1M NCI sales in FY2024 cash flow).","org":{"aliases":[],"country":"US","external_ids":{"cik":null,"companies_house":null,"lei":null,"pic":null,"ror":null,